<section>
<h2>Overlay/modal dialog</h2>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Pay attention to</h2>
<ul>
<li>Focus management</li>
<li>role="dialog" and aria-modal="true" (use authoring practice)</li>
<li>Accessible close button</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Focus management </h2>
<ul>
<li>When opened: move focus to new info</li>
<li>Focus limited to overly only (keyboard trap)</li>
<li>After closing: return focus to original starting point</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>ARIA</h2>
<ul>
<li>role="dialog" because dialog element still lacks overall support</li>
<li>aria-modal="true" to make content outside modal dialog inaccessible</li>
<li>also possible with aria-hidden="true", but cumbersome and risky</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Close button</h2>
<ul>
<li>Meaningful label</li>
<li>Logical reading and tab order</li>
<li>Clearly visible focus</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Example</h2>
<p><a target="tweede" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices-1.1/examples/dialog-modal/dialog.html">Example (WAI ARIA practices)</a></p>

</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Tab panel</h2>
<ul>
<li>Non-existent concept in HTML</li>
<li>Just a list of links and divs</li>
<li>Semantics are added using ARIA</li>
<li>Article: <a target="tweede" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices-1.1/#tabpanel">WAI-ARIA Authoring Practice 1.1 for Tab Panel</a></li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Keyboard</h2>
<ul>
<li>Tabindex="0" for active tab in tablist</li>
<li>Arrows to select different tab</li>
<li>When tab is pressed, focus directs to start of active tab panel</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Role="application"</h2>
<ul>
<li>Creates a application in accessibility tree</li>
<li><a target="tweede" href="https://www.marcozehe.de/if-you-use-the-wai-aria-role-application-please-do-so-wisely/">Use with extreme caution</a></li>
<li>All standard functionalities provided by screenreader are gone</li>
<li>You'll have to program everything yourself</li>
<li>And you have to explain the user how the application works</li>
</ul>
</section>
